    "description": "WorkforceRegistry manages Employee, Engineer, Manager, and Contractor records from a stable domain hierarchy. Every worker shares common details such as name, hire date, department, and status, while each kind has mandatory additional details: engineers require a technical grade, managers require a team size, and contractors require a supplier and contract end date. The registry must frequently load workers across all kinds for directory searches, reporting, and authorization, and callers commonly request all workers of a particular kind. The hierarchy changes infrequently, but additions within a kind are routine. Decide the relational layout that preserves mandatory subtype-specific constraints, avoids duplicating shared attributes, and supports efficient polymorphic retrieval without requiring application code to merge records from several tables.",
    "decision_statement": "Decide how to persist a small, stable worker hierarchy with mostly shared attributes, mandatory kind-specific fields, and frequent retrieval across all kinds.",
    "notes": "A small stable hierarchy with shared attributes and frequent cross-kind reads favors one unified row layout; the per-class and per-concrete layouts stay in play for the mandatory-subtype-field axis."
  },
